## Natural-Language Auto-Detection

When the user does not name a command, route on intent:

| They said | Route to |
|-----------|----------|
| analyze, trace, impact, "how does X work", "where is Y handled" | `/analyze` |
| implement, add, fix, build, wire up | `/implement` |
| review, check, critique, "is this any good" | `/review` |
| test, coverage, spec | `/test` |
| secure, vulnerability, CVE, secret, injection | `/security` |
| decide, tradeoff, "should we", alternative | `/adr` |
| ship, release, cut a version, changelog | `/release` |
| slow, expensive, tokens, context window | `/budget` |
| "what did we decide about", "why is it like this" | `/memory` then `/adr` |
| "what does the client doc say", requirement, spec sheet | `/knowledge` |

Ambiguity between two routes is not a reason to ask. Pick the narrower one, say which
you picked in the header, and let the user redirect in one word.

